melody:
The wa-ter is wide, I can-not get o'er,
D4 G4/ G4/ A4 B4(4) ~B4 A4/ A4/ G4 E4 D4(4) ~D4
and nei-ther have I wings to fly;
D4 G4 F#4 G4(4) ~G4 A4/ B4/ C5 B4 ~A4(4) ~A4
give me a boat that will car-ry two,
A4 B4 C5 D5(4) ~D5 C5/ B4/ A4 G4 B4(4) ~B4
and both shall row, my love and I.
A4 G4 E4 D4(4) ~D4 D4 D4 E4/ ~F#4/ G4(4) ~G4

A ship there is, and she sails the sea,
D4 G4/ G4/ A4 B4(4) ~B4 A4/ A4/ G4 E4 ~D4(4) ~D4
she's load-ed deep as deep can be,
D4 G4 F#4 G4(4) ~G4 A4/ B4/ C5 B4 ~A4(4) ~A4
but not so deep as the love I'm in,
A4 B4 C5 D5(4) ~D5 C5/ B4/ A4 G4 B4(4) ~B4
I know not if I sink or swim.
A4 G4 E4 D4(4) ~D4 D4 D4 E4/ ~F#4/ G4(4) ~G4 r(3)
